1.Lower Bound : Smallest index such that arr[ind]>=x
Brute force: Linear Search , T.C. -> O(N) and S.C. -> O(1)

Optimized Code : as array is sorted , definitely proceed with binary Search and in this lower bound we always hunt for better that's why after getting also answer, we still hunt because there might be possible that I can get better that's why go left -> mid-1
                                                                                                               
code: 

class Solution {
    int lowerBound(int[] arr, int target) {
        int n=arr.length;
        int low=0,high=n-1,ans=n;
        while(low<=high)
        {
            int mid=(low+high)/2;
            if(arr[mid]>=target)
            {
                ans=mid;
                high=mid-1;
            }
            else
            {
                low=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

T.C. -> O(Log2N)

